Count packet loss, keyframe requests and the round trip for the app.

IHS_SessionGetStreamStats returns the video packets received and lost (expected minus
received over the packet ids, as RTP counts it), the data lost notifications sent for video
(Steam answers each with a keyframe), and a smoothed round trip. The round trip comes from
ACKs of reliable packets that were sent once: ihslib resends after 10 ms, so for a resent
packet the ACK could belong to either send. Steam's ACK body holds its own receive time, not
an echo of ours, which can't be compared across machines. The counters live in the session,
so they stay readable after the data channels are gone.

